{"RunId":"d55632e4-65cc-4098-9adb-ad73db4b17e0","Seq":27,"Kind":"NodeCompleted","Synthetic":true,"TimestampUtc":"2026-04-26T09:02:13.9158154Z","NodeId":"n_ym05bcg","NodeName":null,"Payload":{"nodeInstanceId":"0cc03be0-eb56-4841-9b91-5b3f0512269b","duration":"PT1M57.4611251S","inputData":{"triggerType":"WebHook","triggerTime":"2026-04-26T09:00:16.4064612Z","webHookMethod":"POST","webHookRoute":"/webhook/investigate-icm","bodyJsonSchema":"{\n   \u0022type\u0022: \u0022object\u0022,\n   \u0022required\u0022: [\u0022incidentId\u0022, \u0022serviceName\u0022, \u0022teamName\u0022, \u0022timestamp\u0022],\n   \u0022properties\u0022: {\n     \u0022incidentId\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022integer\u0022, \u0022format\u0022: \u0022int64\u0022 },\n     \u0022serviceName\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022string\u0022 },\n     \u0022teamName\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022string\u0022 },\n     \u0022timestamp\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022string\u0022, \u0022format\u0022: \u0022date-time\u0022 }\n   }\n }","messageType":"json","body.timestamp":"2026-04-26T09:00:12.843Z","body.incidentId":784334093,"body.serviceName":"","body.teamName":"","__webhookBody":"{\n  \u0022incidentId\u0022: 784334093,\n  \u0022serviceName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022teamName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022timestamp\u0022: \u00222026-04-26T09:00:12.843Z\u0022\n}"},"outputData":{"mode":"skill","backend":"copilot","model":"claude-sonnet-4.6","agentName":"open-icm","agentSummary":"","result":"Here\u0027s the full investigation summary for **ICM 784334093**:\n\n---\n\n## \uD83D\uDCCB Incident Overview\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Incident ID** | 784334093 |\n| **Title** | [Watson Harmony] Spike in crashes \u2014 Azure Local Edge Observability (Cloud) |\n| **Status** | \uD83D\uDD34 Active |\n| **Severity** | Sev 3 |\n| **Service** | **Azure Stack HCI** |\n| **Team** | **UpdateService** |\n| **Owner** | J Sebastian Rodriguez Galarza (\u0060jrodriguezga\u0060) |\n| **Spike Detected** | 4/22/2026 1:30 PM UTC |\n| **Affected Region** | japaneast (primary) |\n| **Subscription Type** | NonProd |\n\n---\n\n## \uD83D\uDD0D Root Cause Analysis\n\nThis is a **Watson Harmony automated crash spike alert**. The \u0060microsoft.azurestack.updateservice.winsvchost.exe\u0060 process (381 total crashes) spiked sharply. Five crash buckets were identified:\n\n### Top Crash Buckets\n\n| Rank | Crashes | Failure Bucket | Diagnosis |\n|------|---------|----------------|-----------|\n| 1 | **139** | \u0060UnauthorizedAccessException\u0060 \u2192 \u0060TraceEventSession..ctor\u0060 (TraceEvent.dll) | ETW session creation denied \u2014 service account lacks SeSystemProfilePrivilege or admin rights |\n| 2 | **113** | \u0060Win32Exception (0x80004005)\u0060 \u2192 \u0060SafeClusterHandle.OpenClusterHandle\u0060 | Cannot open Windows Failover Cluster API handle \u2014 cluster service may be unreachable or permissions missing |\n| 3 | **59** | \u0060ArgumentException\u0060 \u2192 \u0060UpdateService.Core.dll\u0060 | Invalid argument passed internally in UpdateService core logic |\n| 4 | **36** | \u0060ConnectionFailureException\u0060 \u2192 \u0060Http.Client.Remoting.dll\u0060 | Service-to-service HTTP remoting failures |\n| 5 | **24** | \u0060UnauthorizedAccessException\u0060 \u2192 \u0060UnityConfig.RegisterCaching\u0060 (UpdateService.Service) | IoC container caching setup blocked \u2014 access denied at startup |\n\n### Secondary Faulting Components\n\n| Module / Process | Crash Count |\n|-----------------|-------------|\n| \u0060agentlifecycleagenthost.dll\u0060 | 170 |\n| \u0060microsoft.diagnostics.tracing.traceevent.dll\u0060 | 146 |\n| \u0060microsoft.azurestack.common.infrastructure.http.client.remoting.dll\u0060 | 67 |\n| \u0060downloadservice.winsvchost.exe\u0060 | 36 |\n| \u0060edgecommonclient.dll\u0060 | 12 |\n\n---\n\n## \uD83E\uDDE0 Key Findings\n\n1. **Authorization regression (primary suspect)**: Buckets #1 and #5 both fail with \u0060E_ACCESSDENIED (0x80070005)\u0060. The UpdateService process is losing access to:\n   - Create ETW tracing sessions (\u0060TraceEventSession\u0060)\n   - Register Unity DI caching at service startup\n   This strongly indicates a **service account privilege regression** or a **local security policy change** on the affected nodes in \u0060japaneast\u0060.\n\n2. **Cluster API unavailability**: Bucket #2\u0027s \u0060OpenClusterHandle\u0060 failure means the service cannot communicate with the Windows Failover Cluster. This may be a cascading failure from lost privileges or a transient cluster service outage.\n\n3. **Connection failures (cascading)**: Bucket #4\u0027s HTTP remoting failures are likely downstream effects of the primary access/cluster issues \u2014 the service can\u0027t initialize cleanly and fails to connect to dependencies.\n\n4. **No correlated Ev2 deployment found**: The Watson report shows an empty deployment correlation table \u2014 the spike may be environmentally triggered rather than caused by a new rollout.\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Recommended Next Steps\n\n1. **Acknowledge the ICM** (per Watson guidelines) \u2014 already started per discussion.\n\n2. **Investigate service account permissions** on affected \u0060japaneast\u0060 NonProd nodes:\n   - Verify \u0060SeSystemProfilePrivilege\u0060 and \u0060SeDebugPrivilege\u0060 are granted to the UpdateService account\n   - Check if a Group Policy update recently modified local security policy\n\n3. **Check Windows Failover Cluster service status** on impacted nodes:\n   - Run \u0060Get-ClusterNode\u0060 or \u0060Get-Service ClusSvc\u0060 on \u0060japaneast\u0060 nodes\n   - Confirm the cluster is accessible from the UpdateService process context\n\n4. **Review Watson portal** for the 5 bucket IDs linked in the summary for detailed crash dump analysis\n\n5. **Check for environment changes in \u0060japaneast\u0060** around \u00604/22/2026 1:30 PM UTC\u0060:\n   - OS patching, VM host migration, storage/network changes\n   - Any manual infrastructure ops\n\n6. **If root cause is confirmed as permission regression**, open a remediation work item to restore the required privileges and consider alerting on future policy drift.\n\n7. **Resolve ICM** once the Watson buckets are addressed and crash rate returns to baseline.\n\n---\n\n[OUTPUT:incidentFolder] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\n[OUTPUT:summary.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\summary.md (4 KB)\n[OUTPUT:discussion.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\discussion.md (307 KB)\n[OUTPUT:rca.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\rca.md (6 KB)\n[OUTPUT:metadata.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\metadata.md (1 KB)\n[OUTPUT:ai_summary.md]","ai.success":true,"ai.model":"claude-sonnet-4.6","ai.durationMs":105532,"ai.inputTokens":257537,"ai.outputTokens":3525,"incidentFolder":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093","summary.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\summary.md (4 KB)","discussion.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\discussion.md (307 KB)","rca.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\rca.md (6 KB)","metadata.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\metadata.md (1 KB)"},"globalVariables":{"body.timestamp":"2026-04-26T09:00:12.843Z","codeIssueFile":"","agentFolder":"E:\\work\\hub\\docs\\wiki","__webhookBody":"{\n  \u0022incidentId\u0022: 784334093,\n  \u0022serviceName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022teamName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022timestamp\u0022: \u00222026-04-26T09:00:12.843Z\u0022\n}","repoMdFile":"E:\\work\\hub\\docs\\wiki\\repos.md","body.incidentId":784334093,"rcaFile":"","metadataFile":"","body.serviceName":"","discussionFile":"","mitigationStepsFile":"","body.teamName":"","rootRepoFolder":"E:\\work","incidentId":0,"queryLoopCount":0,"applicableTsgFile":"","incidentFolder":"","etwEventsFile":"","summaryFile.md":"","queryScore":0